cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use aspective in your work, please cite it as below, and cite the
  original paper of each estimator you use (listed in its docstring and in the
  README).
title: "aspective: peer-reviewed variants of classic estimators, with the scikit-learn API"
type: software
abstract: >-
  aspective collects variants of classic estimators that improve on their
  vanilla versions in peer-reviewed studies but never made it into
  scikit-learn: regularized and mixture discriminant analysis, semi-naive
  Bayes, adaptive nearest neighbours, rotation forests and boosting variants,
  model trees, bias-reduced and penalized linear models, MARS and GAMs, and
  anomaly detectors. Every estimator follows the scikit-learn or PyOD API and
  passes a public benchmark gate that tests it for non-inferiority against
  the model it improves on.
authors:
  - family-names: Hennhoefer
    given-names: Oliver
    email: oliver.hennhoefer@mail.de
repository-code: "https://github.com/OliverHennhoefer/aspective"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - machine learning
  - scikit-learn
  - statistics
  - classification
  - regression
  - anomaly detection
  - benchmarking
  - python
